// The seam between the engine's asset loader and idstd's inf_inflate. idem
// used to carry its own address-based DEFLATE decoder here, the way zst_run
// (comp/zst/entry.id) still does its own; that decoder is gone -- idstd's
// copy under core/data/seq/byte/inflate/ is now the only one, since the two
// were a duplicate-logic error the moment both were in one program. inf_init
// and inf_run just move bytes across the store/list boundary idstd's
// api/deflate.id draws.

// idstd builds its Huffman tables inside every inf_inflate call, so there is
// nothing left to prepare ahead of time. Every boot chain still calls this
// (idem_init4, ed_boot8, and the unit tests' own mains), so it stays as the
// seam they already know.
inf_init() {
} return void;
():()
given png_init ():()

// Reads slen bytes at sa, inflates them, and writes up to cap bytes at da --
// the same contract the flat-store decoder kept: the count actually
// written, or -1 if the stream was corrupt (inf_failed) or decoded to more
// than cap allows. png_inf2 (../inflate.id) is the one caller, and needs no
// change: nothing outside this file has to know the decoder moved.
inf_run(int sa, int slen, int da, int cap) {
  int[] inf_src = inf_read(sa, slen);
  int[] inf_dst = inf_inflate(inf_src, 0);
  int inf_n = len(inf_dst);
} chain (int sa, int slen, int da, int cap) {
  int ret_i = 0 - 1;
  if (inf_failed() = 0 && inf_n <= cap) {
    inf_write(inf_dst, da, inf_n);
    ret_i = inf_n;
  }
} return int ret_i;
